From: "qwen.ai[bot]" <qwenlm-intl@service.alibaba.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:53:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/25] Fix PDF vertical/horizontal text-over-formula
 collisions in fpdf2 exporter

Root causes (per diagnosis):
1. Broken caret X/Y math: flush_line() used pdf.ln(baseline) which ignores
   that tall formula images protrude below the baseline -> next line was
   drawn on top of the previous image (vertical pile-up).
2. No block isolation: inline images taller than the text line never grew
   the reserved line height, so lines collapsed onto each other.
3. render_body_line only flushed when a line contained formulas -> plain
   markdown lines continued on the SAME Y as the previous line
   (horizontal overlap of text over text).

Fixes in src/processing/exporter.py (_write_pdf_fpdf2):
- Dynamic per-line height reservation (_line_h): flush_line advances by the
  max height actually consumed by the current line (text or image).
- Block isolation for tall formulas: any formula PNG whose native 300-dpi
  height exceeds the text baseline is emitted on its own centered line and
  the reserved height grows to image height + padding; short symbols stay
  truly inline inside the text line.
- DPI read from PNG metadata instead of hardcoded 300 (scale mismatch fix).
- render_body_line ALWAYS closes the line via flush_line().
- Fault tolerance: internal fpdf2 errors now fall back to reportlab Unicode
  export instead of emitting unreadable garbage or crashing.

Verified: py_compile OK; E2E export produces valid PDF with 13 formula
images and 62 text placements; strict geometric audit of raw content stream
(BT..Td..Tj vs q w 0 0 h x y cm Do rects) shows ZERO text-over-image
overlaps; stress test (60-row table spanning 2 pages, formula in every cell)
also zero overlaps.
